{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a06913d8c67ad2ba1a039a","type":"tool_result","content":"1200\t                    \"Please try again or request to another team member\"\n1201\t                )\n1202\t            else:\n1203\t                error_msg = (\n1204\t                    f\"Error executing tool '{tool_name}' with arguments {json.dumps(arguments)}: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\\n\"\n1205\t                    \"Please try again or use another tool\"\n1206\t                )\n1207\t            raise AgentToolExecutionError(error_msg, self.logger) from e\n1208\t\n1209\t\n1210\tclass CodeAgent(MultiStepAgent):\n1211\t    \"\"\"\n1212\t    In this agent, the tool calls will be formulated by the LLM in code format, then parsed and executed.\n1213\t\n1214\t    Args:\n1215\t        tools (`list[Tool]`): [`Tool`]s that the agent can use.\n1216\t        model (`Model`): Model that will generate the agent's actions.\n1217\t        prompt_templates ([`~agents.PromptTemplates`], *optional*): Prompt templates.\n1218\t        grammar (`dict[str, str]`, *optional*): Grammar used to parse the LLM output.\n1219\t        additional_authorized_imports (`list[str]`, *optional*): Additional authorized imports for the agent.\n1220\t        planning_interval (`int`, *optional*): Interval at which the agent will run a planning step.\n1221\t        executor_type (`str`, default `\"local\"`): Which executor type to use between `\"local\"`, `\"e2b\"`, or `\"docker\"`.\n1222\t        executor_kwargs (`dict`, *optional*): Additional arguments to pass to initialize the executor.\n1223\t        max_print_outputs_length (`int`, *optional*): Maximum length of the print outputs.\n1224\t        stream_outputs (`bool`, *optional*, default `False`): Whether to stream outputs during execution.\n1225\t        **kwargs: Additional keyword arguments.\n1226\t    \"\"\"\n1227\t\n1228\t    def __init__(\n1229\t        self,\n1230\t        tools: list[Tool],\n1231\